{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa46-d728-77c2-9a0a-18bc71689023"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"b453ccc3-4f00-4f8b-a373-9035c9afcdba","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"b453ccc3-4f00-4f8b-a373-9035c9afcdba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b453ccc3-4f00-4f8b-a373-9035c9afcdba"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260916-3p5y8l, status=development)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Verify independent acceptance and exact prospective composition, preserve every unrelated PR entry.\n- [ ] Publish explicitly Ivan-signed commit and verify local/GitHub signatures, prior ancestry and remote exact head.\n- [ ] Observe real exact-head CI to terminal outcome and capture complete success/failure evidence without claiming premature landing.\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260916-3p5y8l\n- **Title:** TASK-260916-3p5y8l: publish-reviewed-native-toolchain-alignment\n- **Parent:** STORY-260916-19w99a\n\n### Description\n\nAfter independent acceptance, compose only reviewed native-toolchain alignment onto current PR6, publish an Ivan-signed commit preserving prior signed ancestry, and observe exact-head hosted checks honestly.\n\n### Scope\n\nReviewed delta publication and CI observation only; no source fixes or main landing\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nPublished tree matches independent prospective composition; signatures and ancestry verified; exact-head hosted checks observed to completion and reported honestly even if a distinct failure remains.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260916-3p5y8l_publish-brief.md\n> Exact reviewed delta publication contract\n\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/TASK-260916-3p5y8l/TASK-260916-3p5y8l_publish-brief.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2489`\n- Content digest: `sha256:3e37fe4d6156256ce08ae35f3f503c7a8047da4fe514c468f51c9258121cc16d`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260916-3p5y8l_accepted-identity.md\n> Authoritative accepted tree and mode correction\n\nBUG-260916-1rqn1c rev3 accepted by independent Astra RUN-260916-8b18ac, evidence review-verdict-rev3.md. Candidate c07adf4a89996b71c627860f7af7c8c392eace6e. Authoritative prospective PR tree1c1ca7ad20e27e03f003cb3ea0bc466db45fe9e0 on inputd45c85d67b78b6578b5cb0821bd2e78217124d30. Producer prospective008148dc is WRONG: it lost executable mode on scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh. Use reviewer exact modes/blobs for all five paths, contract and selector mode100755. Preserve PR board bytes and rest exactly. See full reviewer report; source need not change. Accepted checkpoint obligation retained pending canonical PR delivery/reconciliation; prior integration_base_moved control-root divergence is still present, no manual managedref moves or forbidden finalleafcheckpoint workaround. Do not attempt internal commit as unrelated publication task. Parent owns supported close-landed after actual landing. Continue established detached signed feature composition route authorized by user.\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260916-3p5y8l_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260916-3p5y8l, name=TASK-260916-3p5y8l_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260916-3p5y8l --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n"}}
